cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
title: assaio
abstract: >-
  Open-source, offline-first Go CLI for platform and engineering teams to observe
  AI adoption and usage breadth, compare API-equivalent cost estimates and inspect
  local delivery evidence. It reads logs across Claude Code, Codex CLI, Gemini CLI,
  GitHub Copilot CLI, Cline, and agy CLI. agy is Google's Antigravity CLI.
  Antigravity contributes activity only and is excluded from token and cost figures. Adoption describes
  observed sessions, active days and tool/project breadth, not employee-wide
  percentages. Costs are estimates from public prices, not invoices or reconstructed
  subscription use. Local session-to-commit candidates and optional bounded PR,
  review, latest-head check and separate historical suite/run observations include
  coverage and withheld conclusions. Directional survival checks recent commit
  changes remaining in HEAD without assigning lines to AI sessions. Delivery
  evidence stays local and ephemeral, separate from the optional self-hosted usage
  MVP, and does not establish causal productivity, ROI or AI session outcomes.
authors:
  - name: The assaio Authors
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.38.0
repository-code: https://github.com/assaio/assaio
url: https://github.com/assaio/assaio
date-released: 2026-10-10
